# DrumMania 4th Mix (G*A25 VER. JAA), Konami 2001: a game, from what drmn4m-install left (its NVRAM). Power-on: the
# flash checksums, NOTE 605 (RTC-RAM cleared): Test at 1500. The boot checks and loading, then
# attract. Two coins (one credit) at frame 10800, then Start every 300 frames through the title,
# the caution screen, the mode select (beginner) and the music select (its default). The first
# stage, from frame ~12900, played on the pads: every 12 frames a hi-hat, snare, high tom, low tom, cymbal, or
# hi-hat or snare with the bass pedal; the stage fails, GAME OVER, and attract again.
# The multi-session unit plays the music and answers on SIO1. MAME's unit is an empty stub, so
# main RAM is MAME's only until the game first touches SIO1; the rest checks HIRAKU against itself.
# Hashes the main RAM every frame and snapshots every 60 frames, to compare with MAME.
game drmn4m

hash ram  0x80000000 0x80400000   # 4 MiB main RAM (KSEG0)

at 1500 press "Service Mode" 8   # NOTE 605
at 10800 press "Coin 1" 8
at 10840 press "Coin 1" 8
at 11100 press "1 Player Start" 8
at 11400 press "1 Player Start" 8
at 11700 press "1 Player Start" 8
at 12000 press "1 Player Start" 8
at 12300 press "1 Player Start" 8
at 12600 press "1 Player Start" 8
at 12900 press "1 Player Start" 8

# the first stage
at 13000 press "Hi-Hat" 3
at 13012 press "Snare" 3
at 13024 press "High Tom" 3
at 13036 press "Low Tom" 3
at 13048 press "Cymbal" 3
at 13060 press "Hi-Hat" 3
at 13060 press "Bass Drum" 3
at 13072 press "Snare" 3
